@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title DefaultAlgorithmDetector.detect(&cpg, function) — per-function evidence pipeline
start
:ControlFlowAnalyzer — collect AST loop and
recursion shapes for family signatures;<<#DBE4FF>>
note right
  detect_loops -> Vec<LoopPattern>
  detect_recursion -> Option<RecursionPattern>
  These shapes remain inputs to family detection.
end note
:ComplexityAnalyzer — compute exact legacy
fallback estimate;<<#F1F3F5>>
:Validate intraprocedural function CFG scope;<<#D3F9D8>>
if (CFG edges and valid loop evidence?) then (yes)
  :loop_forest — headers, strict depth,
reducible / irreducible regions;<<#D3F9D8>>
  :loop_induction — IVs and counted
comparison / bound evidence;<<#FFF3BF>>
  :Evidence-aware polynomial degree,
confidence, and justification;<<#C3FAE8>>
else (no)
  :Use exact legacy estimate;<<#F1F3F5>>
endif
:Combine loop evidence with recursion,
keep worse class, and retain subordinate evidence;<<#FFE8CC>>
:Five family heuristics — sorting, searching,
graph, dynamic programming, divide-and-conquer;<<#FCC2D7>>
:DetectedAlgorithm records, sorted by
confidence descending and thresholded;<<#E5DBFF>>
stop
legend right
  |= colour |= pipeline evidence |
  |<#DBE4FF>| semantic AST family shape |
  |<#D3F9D8>| CFG / loop forest |
  |<#FFF3BF>| DFG-backed induction |
  |<#F1F3F5>| exact compatibility fallback |
  |<#C3FAE8>| complexity evidence |
  |<#FFE8CC>| recursion composition |
  |<#FCC2D7>| family heuristics |
  |<#E5DBFF>| public result |
endlegend
@enduml
